   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the uniform city court act, in relation to the residence of\nthe part-time judge of the city court of Lackawanna; and providing for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8780",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8780-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2104, UCCA",
    "lawSection": "Uniform City Court Act",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8780\n\nSPONSOR: JACOBS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the uniform city court act, in relation to the residence\nof the part-time judge of the city court of Lackawanna; and providing\nfor the repeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would allow for a non-resident of Lackawanna to assume to\nposition of the part-time city court judge of Lackawanna.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends section 2104 of the Uniform City Court Act to include\nthe position of part-time judge of the Lackawanna city court within the\npositions that exempt the residency requirement of the law.\n\nSection 2. Allows the act to take effect immediately and \"sunset\" as\nsuch time as the part-time judge appointed during the calendar year 2018\nis no longer employed as the part-time judge for the Lackawanna city\ncourt.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nLackawanna has a limited pool of attorneys from which to draw a poten-\ntial city court judge. The part-time position is unable to be filled\ncurrently by a resident of Lackawanna. It is hoped that this is a tempo-\nrary problem and will not require permanent exemption for the city to\nfill this position.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
